  ('ambiguous', 'adjective: having more than one possible meaning', 'adjective: having more than one possible meaning', 'mơ hồ, nhập nhằng', 'unclear, vague, equivocal', '/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/', 'The coach told his team, "Move to that side of the field," but because he did not point, his directions were ambiguous, and nobody knew where to go.'),
