  ('apparent', 'adjective: clearly seen or understood; adjective: seeming (but not definitely true)', 'adjective: clearly seen or understood; adjective: seeming (but not definitely true)', 'rõ ràng, hiển nhiên', 'evident, obvious, clear', '/əˈpærənt/', 'After only a few months, it was apparent that the French would not win the war.
The shark''s apparent sleepiness is actually because of how cold the water is.'),
  ('apparently', 'according to what seems or is reported to be true', 'according to what seems or is reported to be true', 'dường như, hình như', 'seemingly, reportedly', '/əˈpær.ənt.li/', 'The decision was apparently taken without consultation.'),
  ('append', 'verb: to add to the end', 'verb: to add to the end', 'thêm vào', NULL, NULL, 'Mozart, dissatisfied with the tragic, destructive ending to his opera Don Giovanni, appended a final scene that gives a lighter conclusion.'),
  ('applicable', 'có thể áp dụng, thích hợp', 'relevant or appropriate to a situation', 'có thể áp dụng, thích hợp', 'relevant, pertinent, germane', '/æplɪˈkeɪbəl/', NULL),
  ('apprehension', 'noun: fear that something bad will happen', 'noun: fear that something bad will happen', 'sự lo ngại', NULL, NULL, 'Every time I get on an airplane, I breathe deeply and tell myself it''s safe, but still I have a feeling of apprehension as we take off.'),
  ('apprehensive', NULL, 'worried or frightened that something unpleasant may happen', 'sợ hãi, e sợ', '', '/ˌæprɪˈhensɪv/', 'an apprehensive face/glance/look She was deeply apprehensive that something might go wrong. You have no reason to be apprehensive of the future.'),
  ('apprenticeship', NULL, 'a period of time working as an apprentice; a job as an apprentice', 'sự học việc, sư học nghề; thời gian học việc, thời gian học nghề', '', ' /əˈprentɪʃɪp/', 'She was in the second year of her apprenticeship as a carpenter. He had served his apprenticeship as a plumber. Apprenticeships were becoming more difficult to find.'),
  ('approach', 'verb: to move closer to something or someone; noun: a way to do something', 'verb: to move closer to something or someone; noun: a way to do something', 'phương pháp tiếp cận', NULL, NULL, 'The sign at the park said clearly, "Do not approach wild animals! They will bite."
The new CEO had a very strange approach to management, letting his employees sleep whenever they wanted.'),
  ('approbation', 'sự tán thành, khen ngợi', 'approval or praise', 'sự tán thành, khen ngợi', 'approval, endorsement, praise', '/ˌæprəˈbeɪʃən/', NULL),
  ('apt', 'adjective: perfectly appropriate', 'adjective: perfectly appropriate', 'phù hợp', NULL, NULL, 'The lion is sometimes called "king of the beasts," an apt description given the animal''s appearance and power.'),
