  ('arise', 'phát sinh, nảy sinh', 'to come into being; to emerge or originate', 'phát sinh, nảy sinh', 'emerge, surface, originate', '/əˈraɪz/', 'A new crisis has arisen. We keep them informed of any changes as they arise. Children should be disciplined when the need arises (= when it is necessary). A storm arose during the night.'),
