  ('assemble', 'tập hợp, lắp ráp', 'to gather together; to fit parts together', 'tập hợp, lắp ráp', 'convene, congregate, construct', '/əˈsɛmbəl/', NULL),
  ('assent', 'đồng ý', 'to express approval or agreement', 'đồng ý', 'agree, consent, concur', '/əˈsent/', NULL),
  ('assert', 'khẳng định', 'to state a fact or belief confidently and forcefully', 'khẳng định', 'affirm, declare, contend', '/əˈsɜːrt/', 'assert that… She continued to assert that she was innocent. assert something She continued to assert her innocence. + speech ‘That is wrong,’ he asserted.'),
  ('assertion', 'sự khẳng định, luận điểm', 'a confident and forceful statement of fact or belief', 'sự khẳng định, luận điểm', 'declaration, affirmation, contention', '/əˈsɜːrʃən/', NULL),
  ('assertive', NULL, 'expressing opinions or desires strongly and with confidence, so that people take notice', 'khẳng định, quả quyết, quyết đoán', '', '/əˈsɜːrtɪv/', 'You should try and be more assertive. assertive behaviour'),
  ('assess', 'verb: to look closely at and figure out the value or type of something', 'verb: to look closely at and figure out the value or type of something', 'dánh giá, thẩm định', 'evaluate, appraise, gauge', '/əˈses/', 'Before buying a house, you should always assess the building carefully.'),
  ('asset', NULL, '[ C usually plural ] something valuable belonging to a person or organization', 'thường ở dạng số nhiều) (Số nhiều) Của cải, tài sản, vật thuộc quyền sở hữu.', '', '/ˈæset/', 'A company''s assets can consist of cash, investments, specialist knowledge, or copyright material. Her assets include shares in the company and a house in France. asset sales/management'),
