  ('conservationist', 'nhà bảo tồn', 'a person who advocates protecting the environment', 'nhà bảo tồn', NULL, '/kənˈsɜːrveɪʃənɪst/', NULL),
  ('conservative', NULL, 'opposed to great or sudden social change; showing that you prefer traditional styles and values', 'bảo thủ, thủ cựu', '', ' /kənˈsɜːrvətɪv/', 'a conservative society/outlook Older people tend to be more conservative and a bit suspicious of anything new.'),
  ('conserve', NULL, 'to keep and protect something from damage, change, or waste', 'Giữ gìn, duy trì, bảo tồn, bảo toàn', '', '/kənˈsɜːrv/', 'To conserve electricity, we are cutting down on our heating. The nationalists are very eager to conserve their customs and language. I''m not being lazy - I''m just conserving my energy/strength for later.'),
  ('considerable', 'dáng kể, lớn', 'notably large in size, amount, or extent', 'dáng kể, lớn', 'substantial, significant, sizable', '/kənˈsɪdərəbəl/', 'A considerable number of popular sports were invented in only the last 100 years.'),
  ('considerably', 'một cách đáng kể', 'to a notably large extent', 'một cách đáng kể', 'substantially, significantly, markedly', '/kənˈsɪdərəbli/', NULL),
  ('consideration', 'sự cân nhắc, yếu tố xem xét', 'careful thought; a factor taken into account', 'sự cân nhắc, yếu tố xem xét', 'deliberation, contemplation, reflection', '/kənˈsɪdər.eɪʃən/', NULL),
  ('consist', 'verb: to be made of', 'verb: to be made of', 'bao gồm, cấu thành', 'comprise, constitute, embody', '/kənˈsist/', 'The U.S. consists of fifty states.'),
  ('consistency', NULL, 'the quality of always behaving in the same way or of having the same opinions, standard, etc.', 'sự kiên định, tính trước sau như một; tính nhất quán', '', '/kənˈsɪstənsi/', 'She has played with great consistency all season. We need to ensure the consistency of service to our customers.'),
  ('consistently', 'một cách nhất quán', 'in a way that is regular and unchanging', 'một cách nhất quán', 'reliably, uniformly, steadfastly', '/kənˈsɪstəntli/', NULL),
  ('consolidate', 'củng cố, hợp nhất', 'to combine into a single more effective whole', 'củng cố, hợp nhất', 'strengthen, unify, merge', '/kənˈsɑːlɪdeɪt/', NULL),
  ('consonant', 'phụ âm', 'a speech sound that is not a vowel', 'phụ âm', NULL, '/kənˈsɒnənt/', NULL),
  ('conspicuous', 'adjective: easy to see', 'adjective: easy to see', 'dễ thấy, nổi bật', 'noticeable, prominent, obvious', '/kənˈspɪkjuəs/', '"Just my luck!" said Sam, whose forehead had grown a conspicuous pimple the day before the school dance.'),
  ('conspicuous consumption', NULL, 'null', 'tiêu dùng phô trương', '', '', 'cons_______us co_______ion'),
  ('constant', 'adjective: not changing and not stopping; continuous', 'adjective: not changing and not stopping; continuous', 'hằng số', NULL, NULL, 'The river flows constantly through the year and never freezes.'),
  ('consternation', 'sự bàng hoàng, sửng sốt', 'a feeling of anxiety or dismay', 'sự bàng hoàng, sửng sốt', 'dismay, alarm, distress', '/ˌkɑːnstərˈneɪʃən/', NULL),
  ('constitute', 'verb: to be the pieces that make a whole', 'verb: to be the pieces that make a whole', 'cấu thành, tạo thành', 'comprise, compose, form', '/kənˈstɪtjuːt/', 'Fifty states constitute the U.S.A.'),
  ('constitutional rights', 'quyền hiến định', NULL, 'quyền hiến định', NULL, '/ˌkɒnstɪˈtjuːʃənl raɪts/', NULL),
  ('constrain', 'verb: to limit the activity of; to restrict', 'verb: to limit the activity of; to restrict', 'ép buộc, hạn chế', 'compel, restrict, restrain', '/kənˈstreɪn/', 'Popular belief says that a pet fish''s size is constrained by the size of the tank it''s in, but this is actually false.'),
  ('constraint', 'noun: something that limits or restricts', 'noun: something that limits or restricts', 'ràng buộc, hạn chế', 'limitation, restriction, restraint', '/kənˈstreɪnt/', 'We don''t have many resources, so we''ll have to work with some very tight constraints.'),
  ('constrict', 'thắt chặt, hạn chế', 'to make narrower; to limit', 'thắt chặt, hạn chế', 'restrict, narrow, tighten', '/kənˈstrɪkt/', NULL),
  ('construct', 'xây dựng, kiến tạo', 'to build or form; an idea or theory', 'xây dựng, kiến tạo', 'build, assemble, fabricate', '/kənstrʌkt/', 'The land flooded every year, so it was unsafe to construct buildings on it.'),
  ('consult', 'tham khảo, hỏi ý kiến', 'to seek information or advice from', 'tham khảo, hỏi ý kiến', 'confer, counsel, refer to', '/kənˈsʌlt/', NULL),
  ('consume', 'verb: to eat; verb: to use up (a resource)', 'verb: to eat; verb: to use up (a resource)', 'tiêu thụ, tiêu dùng', 'devour, expend, deplete', '/kənˈsum/', 'Our high living standards cause our current population to consume 25 percent of the world''s oil. We consumed vast quantities of food and drink that night. Alcohol should be consumed in moderation, and this is particularly true for pregnant women.'),
  ('consumption', NULL, 'the act of using energy, food or materials; the amount used', 'Sự tiêu thụ, sự tiêu dùng (hàng hoá, điện, than, nước... ).', '', '/kənˈsʌmpʃn/', 'the production of fuel for domestic consumption (= to be used in the country where it is produced) Gas and oil consumption always increases in cold weather. The meat was declared unfit for human consumption.'),
  ('contact', 'noun: the state of touching; noun: having possible or normal communication; verb: communicating (as by email or phone especially) to give or get specific information', 'noun: the state of touching; noun: having possible or normal communication; verb: communicating (as by email or phone especially) to give or get specific information', 'liên hệ', NULL, NULL, 'An electrical wire in contact with a pool of water can be extremely dangerous.
Liam is still in contact with many of his high-school teachers, surprisingly.
The woman at the help desk told me to contact the student affairs office if I want to change rooms.'),
  ('contagious', NULL, 'a co_______us disease spreads by people touching each other (có khả năng lây lan)', ' ', '', '/kənˈteɪdʒəs/', 'Scarlet fever is highly contagious. The infection is highly contagious, so don''t let anyone else use your towel.'),
  ('container', 'vật chứa, thùng chứa', 'an object used to hold or transport something', 'vật chứa, thùng chứa', 'receptacle, vessel, holder', '/kənˈteɪnər/', NULL),
  ('contaminate', NULL, 'to make a substance or place dirty or no longer pure by adding a substance that is dangerous or carries disease', 'làm bẩn, làm ô uế', '', ' /kənˈtæmɪneɪt/ ', 'The drinking water has become contaminated with lead. a river contaminated by pollution'),
  ('contaminated', NULL, 'to be dirty or poisonous', 'bị bẩn, bị ô uế', '', '/kənˈtæm.ə.neɪ.t̬ɪd/', 'The infection was probably caused by swimming in contaminated water/water contaminated with sewage.'),
  ('contemplate', 'suy ngẫm', 'to think about deeply', 'suy ngẫm', 'ponder, consider, meditate', '/ˈkɑːntəmpleɪ t/', NULL),
  ('contend', 'tranh luận, khẳng định; cạnh tranh', 'to assert or argue; to compete', 'tranh luận, khẳng định; cạnh tranh', 'assert, maintain, argue', '/kənˈtɛnd/', 'I contend that it is impossible — tôi dám chắc rằng cái đó không thể thực hiện được I would contend that the minister''s thinking is flawed on this point. The lawyer contended (that) her client had never been near the scene of the crime.'),
