  ('disaster', NULL, '(an event that results in) great harm, damage, or death, or serious difficulty', 'Tai hoạ, thảm hoạ, tai ách; Điều bất hạnh.', 'catastrophe', '/dɪˈzæstər/', 'An inquiry was ordered into the recent rail disaster (= a serious train accident). It would be a disaster for me if I lost my job. This is one of the worst natural disasters ever to befall the area.'),
  ('disastrous', NULL, 'very bad, harmful or unsuccessful Bất hạnh.', 'Tai hại, thảm khốc.', 'catastrophic, devastating', '/dɪˈzæstrəs/', 'Such a war would be disastrous for the country. This decision will have a disastrous impact on foreign policy. His first attempt was disastrous.'),
