  ('disperse', 'verb: to cause to separate and go in different directions', 'verb: to cause to separate and go in different directions', 'phân tán, giải tán', 'scatter, dissipate, diffuse', '/dɪˈspɜːr/', 'Students came from many countries for English classes at our school, but after the program ended, they dispersed and never saw each other again.'),
