  ('draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('drama', NULL, 'plays considered as a form of literature plays and acting generally', 'Nghệ thuật kịch; nghệ thuật tuồng nói chung', '', '/ˈdrɑːmə/', 'classical/Elizabethan/modern, etc. drama a drama critic drama school a drama student I studied English and Drama at college.'),
  ('dramatic', NULL, '(of a change, an event, etc.) sudden, very great and often surprising exciting and impressive (kịch tích, gay cấn) exaggerated in order to create a special effect and attract people’s attention (cường điệu hóa để thu hút sự chú ý)', 'đột ngột', '', '/drəˈmætɪk/', 'a dramatic increase/fall/change/improvement a dramatic victory He flung out his arms in a dramatic gesture. Don''t be so dramatic!'),
  ('drastically', 'một cách quyết liệt, mạnh mẽ', 'in a severe or extreme manner', 'một cách quyết liệt, mạnh mẽ', 'severely, radically, extremely', '/dræstɪkli/', NULL),
  ('draw the line', NULL, 'If you draw the line at a particular activity you would not do it because you disapprove of it or because it is so extreme.', 'vạch ra ranh giới', '', '', 'I’ll do almost anything – although I think I’d draw the line at running naked across the stage!'),
  ('drawback', 'noun: a disadvantage, a negative part', 'noun: a disadvantage, a negative part', 'nhược điểm', NULL, NULL, 'While the new office was cleaner and in a nicer part of town, the total lack of windows was a major drawback that changed the team''s mind.'),
  ('dreary', 'adjective: sad and boring or colorless', 'adjective: sad and boring or colorless', 'buồn tẻ', NULL, NULL, 'The party was a dreary affair: only five people showed up, and none of them could find much to talk about.'),
  ('drench', 'verb: to cover completely with liquid', 'verb: to cover completely with liquid', 'làm ướt đẫm, tưới đẫm', NULL, NULL, 'We regretted not checking the weather before leaving home when we were quickly drenched by an unexpected summer storm.'),
  ('drive someone up the wall', NULL, '[INFORMAL] annoy someone very much', 'làm ai đó phát điên', '', '', 'He’s so uncooperative he’s beginning to drive me up the wall.'),
  ('drought', 'noun: a long time with not enough rain', 'noun: a long time with not enough rain', 'hạn hán', 'aridity, dryness', '/drɔːt/', 'The drought left the landscape dry and lifeless; it had not rained in months, and even the river that the town depended on for water had dried up.'),
  ('drowsy', 'adjective: sleepy', 'adjective: sleepy', 'buồn ngủ', NULL, NULL, 'The day dragged on, and the only thing keeping the workers from getting drowsy was the automatically refilling coffee machine.'),
  ('dubious', 'adjective: suspicious and possibly wrong', 'adjective: suspicious and possibly wrong', 'đáng ngờ', 'doubtful, questionable, suspect', '/ˈduːbiəs/', 'I saw a carton of milk with an expiration date so dubious I decided to buy it for fun: it has a date one year from today printed on it.'),
  ('due to', 'caused by; because of', 'caused by; because of', 'do, bởi vì', 'owing to, because of', NULL, 'The rise is due to changes in migration.'),
  ('dump', NULL, 'to get rid of something you do not want, especially in a careless way Đổ ầm xuống, ném phịch xuống', 'Đổ thành đống (rác); vứt bỏ, gạt bỏ (ai...', '', ' /dʌmp/', 'Too much toxic waste is being dumped at sea. The dead body was just dumped by the roadside.'),
  ('dung', 'phân động vật', 'the excrement of animals', 'phân động vật', 'manure, excrement', '/dʌŋ/', NULL),
  ('durable', 'adjective: hard to break or damage (in a good way)', 'adjective: hard to break or damage (in a good way)', 'bền bỉ', NULL, NULL, 'Andrew only buys durable shoes—if they can''t survive at least ten years of regular wear, he won''t even consider buying them.'),
  ('duration', 'khoảng thời gian, thời lượng', 'the length of time something continues', 'khoảng thời gian, thời lượng', 'span, period, interval', '/dəˈrɪʃən/', NULL),
  ('dusk', 'noun: the time of day immediately after the sun goes down', 'noun: the time of day immediately after the sun goes down', 'hoàng hôn', NULL, NULL, 'Even though the sun had set and dusk had fallen, Sara and Klaus stayed on the beach, talking and laughing into the night.'),
  ('dwell', 'verb: to live somewhere', 'verb: to live somewhere', 'cư trú; nghiên ngẫm', 'reside, inhabit, abide', '/dwel/', 'Creatures that dwell deep in the darkest caves have lost all color in their skin and become blind from the darkness.'),
  ('dwell on', NULL, 'to keep thinking or talking about something, especially something that would be better to forget', 'Dừng lại ở, chăm chú vào, nhấn lâu vào, day đi day lại, nói đi nói lại.', '', '/dwel/', 'So you made a mistake, but there''s no need to dwell on it.'),
  ('dwelling', 'noun: housing that someone is living in', 'noun: housing that someone is living in', 'nơi ở', NULL, NULL, 'Expecting her lazy boyfriend’s dwelling to be messy, Jane was shocked to find that the apartment was neat and clean.'),
  ('dwindle', 'verb: to become much less or many fewer', 'verb: to become much less or many fewer', 'giảm dần', NULL, NULL, 'Due to repeated overfishing, the numbers of snow crabs have severely dwindled in recent years.'),
  ('dye', NULL, 'to change the colour of something, especially by using a special liquid or substance', 'nhuộm', '', ' /daɪ/ ', 'She dyed her hair blonde. For a change, why not dye your T-shirts? dyed black hair'),
  ('dynamic', 'adjective: able to change; changing frequently', 'adjective: able to change; changing frequently', 'năng động, biến động', 'active, changing, energetic', '/daɪˈnæmɪk/', 'Robin Williams was a dynamic comedian: because of his sharp mind and ability to improvise, even his co-actors didn''t know what he might say next.'),
