  ('flaw', 'khuyết điểm, tì vết', 'a mark or fault that spoils something', 'khuyết điểm, tì vết', 'defect, imperfection, blemish', '/flɔː/', NULL),
  ('flee', 'verb: to run away from danger', 'verb: to run away from danger', 'chạy trốn', NULL, NULL, 'The sight of a shadow crossing over the ground causes many animals to flee in case there is a predator flying above.'),
  ('fleeting', 'adjective: lasting for a very short time', 'adjective: lasting for a very short time', 'lướt nhanh, thoáng qua; phù du', '', ' /ˈfliːtɪŋ/', 'a fleeting glimpse/smile a fleeting moment of happiness We paid a fleeting visit to Paris.'),
  ('flint', 'đá lửa', 'a hard stone that produces sparks when struck', 'đá lửa', NULL, '/flɪnt/', NULL),
  ('flooding', NULL, 'large amounts of water covering an area that is usually dry; the fact of this happening', 'sự làm ngập lụt; sự úng lụt; nạn lụt', '', ' /ˈflʌdɪŋ/ ', 'There will be heavy rain with flooding in some areas. to cause/prevent flooding severe/widespread flooding'),
  ('floral', 'thuộc hoa, hoa văn', 'relating to flowers', 'thuộc hoa, hoa văn', 'flowered, blossoming', '/ˈflɔːrəl/', NULL),
  ('flourish', 'verb: to grow stronger or healthier', 'verb: to grow stronger or healthier', 'phát triển mạnh, hưng thịnh', 'thrive, prosper, burgeon', '/flaɪr/', 'Few businesses are flourishing in the present economic climate. The arts began to flourish at that time. There was a flourishing black market.'),
  ('flow', NULL, '(of liquid, gas or electricity) to move steadily and continuously in one direction', 'chảy, chạy', '', '/floʊ/', 'She lost control and the tears began to flow. It''s here that the river flows down into the ocean. Blood flowed from a cut on her head. This can prevent air from flowing freely to the lungs. the electric currents flowing through the cables'),
