  ('frantic', NULL, 'done or arranged in a hurry and a state of excitement or confusion', 'Điên cuồng, điên rồ, cuống cuồng', '', '/ˈfræntɪk/', 'They made frantic attempts to revive him. Things are frantic in the office right now.'),
  ('fraudulent', 'adjective: fake or untrue (generally of illegal claims)', 'adjective: fake or untrue (generally of illegal claims)', 'gian lận', NULL, NULL, 'Since I have no background in medicine, If I advertised my services as a doctor, I''d soon be arrested for making the fraudulent claim.'),
