  ('hurdle', NULL, 'a problem that you have to deal with before you can make progress', 'Nghĩa bóng) Vật chướng ngại.', 'obstacle', ' /ˈhɜːrdl/', 'Getting a work permit was the first hurdle to overcome. The cost of this exercise is proving to be a major hurdle.'),
