  ('paradox', 'noun: a situation that seems impossible because it is made of opposite things', 'noun: a situation that seems impossible because it is made of opposite things', 'nghịch lý', NULL, NULL, 'When he first arrived in the desert, Alex did not believe the paradox that drinking hot tea could make a person feel cool.'),
